 // Worked narrative examples match each lesson's actual context, not the old helper defaults.
 const examples={
 V02:'A recorded commute has distance_km=2 and minutes=10. Its labels say Distance (km) and Travel time (minutes); they describe the plotted measurements without renaming either column.',
 V03:'A Wetland survey with area_ha=2 and birds=18 appears at (2, 18) in the Wetland colour. A constant color would remove habitat information; mapping size would add an unneeded cue.',
 V04:'Stone diameters [2, 3, 3, 5, 8, 9, 10, 15] remain the same stones whether the histogram has four bins or two. A coarser view changes intervals, not observations.',
 V05:'Eight page response checks can illustrate a smoothed curve. Changing bw_adjust from 1 to 2 broadens smoothing; the apparent right tail is not reliable population evidence.',
 V06:'Battery trials [2, 4, 4, 6, 8, 10] give an at-or-below proportion 3/6 at four hours and a strictly-above proportion 3/6. Both four-hour batteries remain in the denominator.',
 V07:'Soil conductivity [1.1, 1.4, 1.4, 1.7, 2.2, 2.8] produces six rug marks, including two marks at 1.4 that overlap.',
 V08:'Fiction, Science, Fiction counts returned books as Fiction=2 and Science=1. Summing their late days would answer a different question.',
 V09:'Local fares [2, 2, 3, 9] have mean 4, median 2.5 and count 4. A ticket-average question and a middle-fare question require different summaries.',
 V10:'Beam materials A and B both have mean load 10, but B values [4, 10, 16] spread farther than A values [8, 10, 12]. SD describes those observed differences.',
 V11:'A circuit that lasted 30 hours remains a tested circuit when flagged beyond a box whisker. The flag invites investigation; it does not justify deleting that lifetime.',
 V12:'Three worm lengths in one habitat can illustrate a violin call. Showing the points exposes how little evidence supports its smooth outline.',
 V13:'Sensor A has two separate checks at offset=2. Jitter moves their category-direction positions; their measured offsets remain exactly 2.',
 V14:'Lot A contains three bolts measuring 10 mm. A swarm packs all three at length 10 rather than deleting duplicates or adding random measured-axis noise.',
 V15:'Ink flow readings [3, 7, 7] are three trials. Replacing a density draft with raw points keeps all three, including the coincident pair.',
 V16:'A chamber test with volume_ml=9 and pressure_kpa=20 appears at (9, 20). Sorting pressure separately from volume would invent test pairs.',
 V17:'An exposure can be a Wide-instrument colour and marker shape while marker area represents area_cm2. This repeats instrument identity across two cues and adds one separate physical measurement.',
 V20:'A calibration line fitted to Reference batch must use only its Reference known/read pairs. Including Trial pairs would answer a pooled calibration question.',
 V21:'A spring measured at extension 12 when the line predicts 10 has residual +2. Passing extension to residplot lets it fit and compute deviations; passing an already calculated residual would fit another model.',
 V22:'A light–height matrix cell contains their measured correlation. sample_id identifies a plant; its numeric storage does not make it a scientific variable.',
 V23:'Two museum entries at door East with ticket Adult make count 2. A heatmap colours that supplied count, rather than automatically deciding what each cell means.',
 V24:'The pH histogram counts samples, while the pH/conductivity scatter pairs measurements from those same samples. Assigning each view its own Axes preserves both meanings.',
 V25:'Two production lines share some minutes/units pairs. Colour plus shape keeps line identity available; transparency can expose overlap without moving either measurement.',
 V27:'The centrifuge yield observations have mean 7 and median 5.5. Both are horizontal y benchmarks; median rpm belongs to a vertical x benchmark.',
 V28:'The smallest-area panel is the 2 m² panel that produced 22 W. Annotate (2, 22), not the smallest area combined with another panel’s output.',
 V29:'North delivery boxes [2, 8] have mean 5 and total 10. ax.bar uses whichever heights you calculate; it does not choose the summary for you.',
 V31:'Lake sample identity is separate from oxygen, temperature and depth. Selected pair panels and histogram diagonals summarize measured evidence on the grid’s own Figure.',
 V32:'A train arrival pairs delay_minutes with passengers in the central panel. The top and side panels show each measurement separately; a central benchmark should leave those margins intact.',
 V33:'Workshop relationship panels pair coating time with thickness. Category-distribution panels compare thickness by method; a one-variable histogram panel answers another question.',
 V34:'A finished report scatter can be exported directly. A cramped histogram needs layout repair first; incomplete labels need finishing before the same 150 dpi PNG handoff.',
 V36:'Mean travel costs 3 and 7 have a ratio 3:7. Starting bars at 2 makes visible lengths 1 and 5; zero restores the magnitude comparison.'
 };
